config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_SERVER
	bool "KlaussCPU VNC (RFB) server"
	default n
	depends on NET_SOCKETS
	help
	  Minimal RFB (VNC) server on port 5900 exposing an in-RAM RGB565
	  framebuffer to standard VNC clients (macOS Screen Sharing, TigerVNC,
	  RealVNC).  No VGA hardware required — the framebuffer is served over
	  the network instead of scanned out to a monitor.  Implements the
	  RFB 3.8 mandatory subset (security None, Raw encoding) with per-pixel
	  format conversion.  No auth or TLS — intended for trusted LAN use.

config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_DEMO
	bool "VNC built-in demo content (test pattern + bouncing box)"
	default y
	depends on KLAUSSCPU_VNC_SERVER
	help
	  Draw a test pattern at start and animate a bouncing box so the VNC
	  pipeline has visible content when nothing else drives the framebuffer.
	  Disable when another component (e.g. the Doom app) owns the framebuffer.

config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_PROFILE
	bool "Profile VNC send throughput"
	default n
	depends on KLAUSSCPU_VNC_SERVER
	help
	  Print periodic per-update send time, bytes/update and throughput to the
	  console.  Diagnostic only.

config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_DISPLAY
	bool "Expose the VNC framebuffer as a Zephyr display device"
	default n
	depends on KLAUSSCPU_VNC_SERVER && DISPLAY
	help
	  Register a Zephyr display driver (compatible "klausscpu,vnc-display")
	  whose write() copies into the VNC framebuffer, so display-based stacks
	  such as LVGL render over VNC.  Requires a matching devicetree node set
	  as chosen zephyr,display.

config KLAUSSCPU_VNC_BLITTER
	bool "Offload the display flush copy to the 2D DMA blitter"
	default y
	depends on KLAUSSCPU_VNC_DISPLAY
	help
	  Use the KlaussCPU 2D DMA blitter (MMIO 0xF00E_0000) to copy flushed
	  rectangles from the LVGL draw buffer into the framebuffer, bracketed
	  with whole-cache FLUSH/INVALIDATE for coherency, instead of a CPU
	  memcpy.  Presence is probed at init; if no blitter is in the loaded
	  bitstream the driver transparently falls back to the memcpy, so the
	  same image runs either way.  Set n to force the memcpy path (useful
	  for an A/B baseline on a blitter-equipped bitstream).
